 "result_text": "I changed the Uylings variant of `partition_asymmetry` in `neurom/features/bifurcation.py`. I haven't run any tests or tried it on a morphology.\n\nYou were right: the old code counted every node in each child subtree. At a bifurcation whose children are leaves, that gave `n + m = 2`, which tripped the `n + m <= 2` check and raised `NeuroMError`.\n\nWith `uylings=True` it now:\n- counts the terminal tips in each child subtree (using `ileaf()`) instead of all nodes;\n- returns `abs(n - m) / abs(n + m - 2)`, as before;\n- returns `0.0` when `n + m == 2`, since two terminal tips are trivially symmetric. It no longer raises.\n\nI did not touch the default (non-Uylings) calculation. It still counts all nodes in each child subtree.\n\nThe `n + m == 2` case returning `0.0` is my reading of the Uylings definition, so check it against the paper if you want to be sure.",
